(; constants used by Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Factorial, declared with their translated types ;)

(; doc: `m` and `n` are coprime, or relatively prime, if their `gcd` is 1. ;)
(; //LEAN:Nat.Coprime ;)
Nat__Coprime : (m : Elem Nat) -> (n : Elem Nat) -> Prop.

(; doc: `n.descFactorial k = n! / (n - k)!` (as seen in `Nat.descFactorial_eq_div`), but implemented recursively to allow for "quick" computation when using `norm_num`. This is closely related to `descPochhammer`, but much less general. ;)
(; //LEAN:Nat.descFactorial ;)
Nat__descFactorial : (n : Elem Nat) -> (x : Elem Nat) -> Elem Nat.

(; doc: Returns the smallest prime factor of `n ≠ 1`. ;)
(; //LEAN:Nat.minFac ;)
Nat__minFac : (n : Elem Nat) -> Elem Nat.

